      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Research suggests that a single dose of 5-10 grams of leucine can be sufficient to activate the mTOR pathway initially, rather than a specific threshold within a meal. However, a more chronic dose of 20-30 grams of leucine per day can maintain the signal for protein synthesis.\n\nIf a client is struggling to meet caloric needs, I would recommend increasing the frequency of meals to 5-6 times a day, with a focus on nutrient-dense foods such as lean proteins, complex carbohydrates, and healthy fats. This can help maintain a positive nitrogen balance and support muscle growth, even if individual meal portions are smaller. Higher density foods can also help, as they provide more nutrients per gram of food and can compensate for decreased caloric intake due to smaller portion sizes.",
